Subject: Optimize-Scheduler-Task-Execution

Author: VeltisMC Development Team
Date: 2026-06-19

Reason:
Vanilla scheduler tasks (BukkitScheduler) add task objects to a
priority queue and tick through them on the main thread. For servers
with many scheduled tasks (hundreds of plugins each scheduling
repeating tasks), the per-tick overhead of checking and executing
tasks becomes significant.

Impact:
Lower per-tick overhead from scheduler checks. Better TPS stability
on servers with many plugins.

Migration Note:
This patch optimizes the server's internal scheduler to reduce
per-tick overhead. The actual VeltisMC scheduler implementation
is in the runtime module (DefaultTaskScheduler, PluginScheduler),
which uses virtual threads and avoids main-thread task dispatch
overhead.
